  "title": "Deterministic context win 1: send spec, acceptance and scope once per execute prompt (packet only), all three render call sites (v2)",
  "spec": "P0 audit finding (docs/context-economy/00-audit.md, plan.md): every execute prompt carries spec, acceptance and scope twice: once inside the packet built by spawn._packet_body (sections objective \"- discovery: {spec}\", acceptance, write_scope; spawn.py ~286-305) and again as literal lines in .orchestrator/prompts/execute.md (the three lines starting \"Spec:\", \"Acceptance:\" and \"Scope (only these paths):\", each holding the double-brace placeholder of the same name). The P1 telemetry (merged before this task; context field on runs, per-section meta) is the before/after measure.\nDo:\n1. .orchestrator/prompts/execute.md: remove the three literal lines. Replace with one line: \"The packet above is the task contract: implement the ## objective, satisfy every line of ## acceptance, and edit only paths listed in ## write_scope.\" Keep every other instruction line verbatim (gate loop, commit, unittest rules, _harness rule, dependencies, tool-call budget).\n2. spawn.render: execute no longer needs spec/acceptance/scope kwargs. Update the three call sites so they pass only packet= (spawn.py:773-774 run_worker, daemon.py:561 _dispatch_fresh_fix, daemon.py:853 dispatch). render()'s unfilled-placeholder check must still pass (no leftover double-brace tokens) and extra kwargs must not be silently required; if any call site appends more text after render (spawn.py:774 `+ \\`), keep that text.\n3. Packet guarantee: _packet_body must keep objective (with the full spec), acceptance and write_scope untrimmable even when the packet is over the 4800-char cap (they already are: trimmable = dependencies, evidence, decisions, gotchas, symbols, relevant_tests). Add a regression test that a task with a 9000-char spec and 6 acceptance lines still has every acceptance line and the full spec text and every scope path in the rendered execute prompt exactly once.\n4. Fix-round path: _dispatch_fresh_fix renders execute for the fix task; the fix task's spec is the fix-round spec (failures + acceptance). Verify the packet's objective carries it and nothing is lost; the repair delta path (executor.reply) is unaffected.\n5. Update P1 telemetry expectations if a test in tests/test_spawn.py or tests/test_daemon.py asserts on instruction tokens or on the literal \"Spec:\" line; adjust the expected numbers, never weaken the assertion shape.\n6. Record the measured delta in docs/context-economy/03-dedup-execute-prompt.md (\u226430 lines): chars and est_tokens of the execute prompt for one representative task before and after (use spawn.packet_run_meta or the P1 section meta on a fixture task), and the revert path (git revert the commit).\nTests: tests/test_spawn.py::test_execute_prompt_carries_contract_once (spec, each acceptance line and each scope path appear exactly once in the rendered prompt; no \"Spec:\" literal); tests/test_daemon.py::test_fresh_fix_prompt_renders_without_contract_kwargs (the fresh-fix render path succeeds and the prompt contains the fix spec once). Do not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.\n\nv2 (2026-09-22 16:35): re-filed because v1's spec quoted literal double-brace placeholders, which spawn.render rejects (unfilled_placeholder); never quote them in a spec.",
